      {
        "id": 71655,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-30T13:43:06.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>1v1 it is Omnitron-X and Legacy stomp RA, Ra stomps everyone else. &nbsp;There are a few decent matchups, but the real fun is in 2v2 or 1v1v1, or in the F4 vs. Wardens fight, that was fun but long.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>In multi hero games Argent dies fast, because you want him dead before he gets going. &nbsp;Wraith and Smoke Bombs really helps him, unity and AZ stay alive.</p><p>There are so far two baic rule differences which change the game significantly:</p><p>If you use an Environment deck (I prefer this way) then any card that destroys ongoing also destroys equipment. &nbsp;Play that the choice of what gets destroyed is the hero who played the destruction's choice.</p><p>If you don't use an environment deck then change environment to be Equipment.</p><p>I put my rules and a bit of what I've found out here:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/pvp-training-room-fun-3859\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://greaterthangames.com/forum/topic/pvp-training-room-fun-3859</a></p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:50:53.382Z",
