      {
        "id": 71658,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-31T13:48:30.000Z",
        "cooked": "<blockquote><p><span>I'm interested to see how the theme of SotM comes to the minis arena--the interview Christopher gave on The Spiel made it sound like both companies are really on the same page in trying to bring the comic book feel to the game, so that's a big plus for me. &nbsp;I do wonder exactly \"how far\" they're going to go in terms of expansions--as in, are we going to see Fixer/Expatriette, Nightmist/Argent Adept, and Chrono-Ranger/Omnitron X? &nbsp;Or, are we going to be sticking with the \"core\" Heroes?</span></p></blockquote><p>I imagine some heroes will be very hard to translate to the tactics game, and even if they do, they won't be nearly as cool to play.</p><p>Imagine Argent Adept in a tactics game, they aren't likely to have chains of powers, Adept isn't going to be enarly as awesome as he can be in a card game.</p><p>I'd go with th Scholar, Visionary and Nightmist too, no way they can be like they are in the card game and maintain Balance in a tactical game.</p><p>On the same note though, how cool is Bunker going to be? &nbsp;He'll probably be much more powerful in the tactical game than he is in the card game. &nbsp;I hope they have a turret mode where he gives up movement to use an extra power.</p><p>Unity would be amazing in a tactical game, adding turrets to a hex map, and little Chompers running about biting people's kneecaps off. &nbsp;Don't even know what they'd do with the F5 bots.</p><p>What would you do with Mr. Fixer, or Expat to make them different from other heroes and still good?</p><p>I don't see them being able to make them all in the tactics game, and a good number of the heroes are going to have a very different feel from the card game. &nbsp;Not just the obvious difference in cards vs. map play either, I imagine Legacy isn't going to be as much of a tank as a melee fighter in Tactics.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
