      {
        "id": 71659,
        "name": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-31T20:04:35.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<blockquote>\nI'm interested to see how the theme of SotM comes to the minis arena--the interview Christopher gave on The Spiel made it sound like both companies are really on the same page in trying to bring the comic book feel to the game, so that's a big plus for me. &nbsp;I do wonder exactly \"how far\" they're going to go in terms of expansions--as in, are we going to see Fixer/Expatriette, Nightmist/Argent Adept, and Chrono-Ranger/Omnitron X? &nbsp;Or, are we going to be sticking with the \"core\" Heroes?\n</blockquote>\nWhat would you do with Mr. Fixer, or Expat to make them different from other heroes and still good?\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I could see Fixer as a sort of skirmish-style fighter, almost similar to Tachyon in the sense that he'd be able to hit and run. &nbsp;I could see him doing a bit more damage and being slightly less mobile. &nbsp;I could also see him as a master of manipulating his foes: &nbsp;maybe after he deals damage, he can move a foe to a different adjacent hex or push them away from him. &nbsp;Since the tactics game only allows two Powers, Fixer's deck could almost be ported in as is: &nbsp;one Style, one Tool allowed. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>Expatriette is a bit of a different story, I think. &nbsp;Obviously, her schtick is ranged attacking, but diversity in the card game comes through her weapons. &nbsp;Perhaps something like this:</p>\n<ul><li>Pride and Prejudice: &nbsp;Moderate Range, target two separate foes with a bonus die for accuracy (since they are her signature weapons)</li><li>RPG Launcher: &nbsp;Long distance, cannot be used on foes within X hexes. &nbsp;Choose 1 hex: attacks all foes in or adjacent to that hex.</li><li>Shotgun: Very short range (maybe only adjacent); Heavy damage and pushes foe 1 hex away.</li><li>Hairtrigger Reflexes: any foe that enters Expatriette's LoS, she gets a free attack against. (This would make her into a stealthy sort of character, who ducks behind terrain only to blow you away each time you try to follow)</li><li>Napalm Launcher: &nbsp;Leaves behind a trail of fire in X hexes for one turn, damaging any who enter it. (Good for battlefield control)</li><li>Taser: &nbsp;Moderate distance with low damage. &nbsp;If used to target a minion-type creature, that creature cannot act next round.</li></ul>\n&nbsp;\n<p>Just a few ideas off the top of my head.</p>",
